# Line endings.
#
# This repository is written on Windows and runs on Linux, and zdeploy ships
# the WORKING TREE rather than the index - so whatever `git checkout` puts on
# disk is what lands on the server. Without this file, core.autocrlf=true gives
# every text file CRLF locally, and a shell script with a CRLF shebang fails on
# Linux with the famously unhelpful:
#
#     /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#
# That is exactly how the corrected backup scripts arrived on the box unable to
# run. Anyone cloning this on Windows would hit the same thing, which matters
# more now the repository is public.

# Normalise everything in the repository; let git pick the working-tree form
# unless a rule below says otherwise.
* text=auto

# Executed on Linux. LF is not a preference here, it is a requirement.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Generated by scripts/md_txt.py, which writes LF. Without this the twins show
# as modified on every run - a whole-file diff that hides the real change and
# has to be discarded by hand each time.
*.txt text eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
